# Network secrets / API credentials for the ACME simulation cloud environment.
#
# None are needed for v1:
#   AWS: requests are signed with the key (SigV4), so a header the proxy adds
#     can't authenticate them. The key goes in Environment variables as
#     ACME_AWS_* (see .env.example).
#   GitHub: the GitHub proxy authenticates git and the GitHub tools with the
#     Claude GitHub App. Leave GH_TOKEN / GITHUB_TOKEN unset.
#   Honeycomb, Slack: use claude.ai connectors (Honeycomb's EU MCP server is
#     https://mcp.eu1.honeycomb.io/mcp, added as a custom connector), not
#     tokens in the environment.
#
# Never commit real values.
